// Single responsibility: Liquid-glass rebuild — the same Aurora page as
// `examples/liquid_glass`, but every glass card wears an inline
// `material={|geo| ...}` surface composed from DSL builders only. No
// `GlassPreset`, no preset module import, no `mat_*`/`glass_body`
// helpers: the box shape feeds the material —
// `Lens::beveled(8.0, geo.radius())` bands the bevel dome to the card's
// own corner radius (uniform slot 8, zero recompile on radius edits),
// and the rounded-rect SDF in `ctx_edge_dist_at` bends the dome over
// the actual arcs (capsule ends, 24/32/16 corners alike).
//
// `Lens::beveled` is `#[deprecated]`-marked (the dome profile only
// exists there — `geo.bevel()` is the constant-slope field the header
// rejects); this file carries the one `#[allow(deprecated)]`.
// #[allow(deprecated)] on the closure bodies (one per card) keeps the
// lint local to the call sites.
//
// Surface props (recipe knobs per card):
//   frost = Transmit quad-tap radius (≈ 1.5× the old Gaussian σ),
//   disperse = chromatic fan px (PRISM only),
//   wash_rgb/wash_w = flat mix toward the colour at the wash alpha
//     (the preset wash; dark cards mix toward near-black, BOUNDED —
//     never Beer),
//   spec_rough/spec_gain = GGX lobe roughness and rim/fresnel gain,
//     riding in on the Schlick weight.
// preset_shadow stays (shared renderer path).
//
// Human judges equivalence. Predictions are in the handoff, not claims.

